    "evidence_text": "Arcade (TV series)\n\n The series then ran five nights a week, Mondays to Fridays, as a 30-minute serial.\n\nTina Baker\n\nCompact (TV series)\n\nCompact was a British television soap opera shown by the BBC from 1962 to 1965.\n\n The series was created by Hazel Adair and Peter Ling, who together subsequently devised \"Crossroads\".\n\nHollyoaks\n\nHollyoaks is a British soap opera, first broadcast on Channel 4 on 23 October 1995.\n\n It was originally devised by Phil Redmond, who had previously conceived the Channel 4 soap \"Brookside\".\n\n It is mostly filmed and produced in Childwall, Liverpool, although nearby locations are sometimes used.\n\n It is also popular around the world.\n\nClare Devine\n\n She later returned to the show in 2013.\n\n Bissix has won three British Soap Awards for her portrayal of Clare.\n\n She has also been named one of the best British soap opera characters.\n\nCoronation Street\n\nEpisode 4466\n\n It was accompanied by a special, one-off BBC Red Button episode called \"Billy's Olympic Nightmare\".\n\nCrazy for You (TV series)\n\nPippa Hinchley\n\nPhilippa (Pippa) Lucy Hinchley (born 7 April 1966) is an English actress who played Elaine Fenwick in \"Coronation Street\".\n\nParadise Falls\n\n It was set in a summer cottage community in Muskoka.",
